      },
      {
        "question_text": "$P(x)=2x-3$ and $Q(x)=x^{2}+x-2$.\nFind $P(x)Q(x)+3Q(x)$.",
        "structure": "combined-operations",
        "solution_text": "$P(x)Q(x)+3Q(x)$\n$=(2x-3)(x^{2}+x-2)+3(x^{2}+x-2)$\n$=2x^{3}+2x^{2}-4x-3x^{2}-3x+6+3x^{2}+3x-6$\n$=2x^{3}+2x^{2}-4x$"
      },
