      {
        "question_text": "$P(x)=x^{3}+ax^{2}-2$ and $Q(x)=2x^{3}-5x^{2}+7$.\nIf $P(x)+Q(x)=3x^{3}-x^{2}+5$, find the value of $a$.",
        "structure": "solve-for-coefficient",
        "solution_text": "$P(x)+Q(x)$\n$=(x^{3}+ax^{2}-2)+(2x^{3}-5x^{2}+7)$\n$=3x^{3}+(a-5)x^{2}+5$\nComparing with $3x^{3}-x^{2}+5$, $a-5=-1$\n$a=4$"
      }
